{# Shared skeleton for both generated documents. Bible §15.

   Structure only. Every sentence on the page arrives in the context from
   `documents/copy.py`; nothing here may state a fact, legal or otherwise.

   `.running-footer` is a running element (CSS GCPM): WeasyPrint lifts it out of the flow
   and prints it in the bottom margin of every page. That is how the disclaimer bible §5
   requires reaches all of them without being repeated in the CSS, where it could drift
   out of step with the copy module.

   `footer_extra` is for anything else that belongs in the margin rather than in the body.
   The affidavit puts its "prepared by" line there: at the end of the text it was a single
   orphaned line that pushed a fourth page after the notary block, which is not something
   to hand to a court. #}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<meta name="author" content="{{ product }}">
<meta name="dcterms.created" content="{{ generated_iso }}">
{% block meta %}{% endblock %}
</head>
<body class="{% block body_class %}{% endblock %}">
<div class="running-footer">
	<div>{{ disclaimer }}</div>
	{% block footer_extra %}{% endblock %}
</div>
{% block content %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
